            deeper: "Weakness of the palate, tongue, and neck muscles on the same side, with hoarseness and difficulty swallowing ([[dysphagia|dysphagia]]), points to the lower cranial nerves where they run close together at the skull base or in the upper neck, and needs imaging. Wasting and fasciculation of both sides of the tongue raise concern for motor neuron disease.",
