      presentation: "hoarse-voice-tongue-deviation",
      usage: ["lesson", "review", "challenge"],
      vignette: "A 49-year-old has two weeks of a hoarse voice and difficulty swallowing that began after right-sided neck pain. On saying \"ah,\" the uvula is pulled to the left and the right side of the palate barely rises. The protruded tongue deviates to the right, and the right half of the tongue is wasted with fasciculations while it lies at rest in the mouth.",
