      rationale: "Precise documentation records each test and its result, so the next examiner can repeat it and recognize change. Abbreviations such as \"PERRLA\" miss a [[relative-afferent-pupillary-defect|relative afferent pupillary defect]], which occurs with equal, reactive pupils. Keep findings ([[clinical-sign|signs]]) separate from the interpretation.",
